values ('f5a6b7c8-9d0e-4a95-8b45-6c7d8e9f0a55', 'globalization-and-society', 'Globalization and Society', 'Treat globalization as a set of connected social processes rather than a slogan: flows of people, capital, culture, data, institutions, risk, and power. Contemporary globalization grows out of older histories of conquest, trade, slavery, migration, industrial capitalism, and world-system formation. Students use theoretical tools to explain global interdependence, domination, resistance, and social change across markets, labor, states, institutions, migration, culture, inequality, cities, development, climate, movements, and the question of how societies can govern interdependence more justly.');

