formation, and polarization"}], "description": "This subtopic analyzes political responses to inequality, migration, cultural change, and perceived loss of control."}, {"id": "7ebd0156-ad56-46b3-9546-7d7afa47091e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transnational movements and advocacy", "children": [{"id": "40a30d5f-30bf-4bf6-a1a4-25ace218da6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Feminist, climate, Indigenous, labor, and human rights networks"}, {"id": "dcee7ad7-3d60-4be8-8164-687af0de99e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital mobilization and platform risks"}, {"id": "0fcb01d3-7c2d-4146-b20e-8998f1a76904", "type": "concept", "title": "Coalitions, framing, and strategy"}], "description": "Students learn how movements coordinate across borders while negotiating difference and power."}]}, {"id": "56123609-3f71-4f97-a22d-59d1042833db", "type": "topic", "title": "Futures of Globalization: Digital Networks, AI, Pandemics, De-Risking, and Capstone Case Analysis", "description": "The course ends by asking students to analyze where globalization is going and how societies can govern interdependence more justly.", "children": [{"id": "9fb453d9-eda5-4284-ab60-376ec6f6991b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital globalization and data power", "children": [{"id": "9379ef87-6eb4-4960-8007-aff336ddd29c", "type": "concept", "title": "Data centers, cloud platforms, chips, and undersea cables"}, {"id": "2f725950-2284-4da4-a09b-e8d3672aa957", "type": "concept", "title": "AI, automation, algorithmic governance, and bias"}, {"id": "1d34ef84-a6d3-443b-91e9-b1d26aba4539", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital divides and platform sovereignty"}], "description": "Students examine how digital infrastructure reshapes markets, surveillance, culture, and inequality."}, {"id": "d4665e61-df4b-4c88-a4a8-5ca5432c35b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Risk, resilience, and de-globalization debates", "children": [{"id": "8f14ee66-22e1-448f-b5d3-c4de0e4a9d72", "type": "concept", "title": "Pandemics and global he